  "text": "We are given the functional equation:\n\n$$\nf(x - y) + f(y - z) + f(z - x) + 3xyz = f(x + y) + f(y + z) + f(z + x)\n$$\n\nWe are to find the value of $ f(15) $.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Try simple values\n\nLet’s try $ x = y = z $. Then:\n\n- Left-hand side:  \n  $$\n  f(x - x) + f(x - x) + f(x - x) + 3x \\cdot x \\cdot x = f(0) + f(0) + f(0) + 3x^3 = 3f(0) + 3x^3\n  $$\n\n- Right-hand side:  \n  $$\n  f(x + x) + f(x + x) + f(x + x) = f(2x) + f(2x) + f(2x) = 3f(2x)\n  $$\n\nSo we have:\n$$\n3f(0) + 3x^3 = 3f(2x) \\Rightarrow f(2x) = f(0) + x^3\n$$\n\nThis suggests that $ f $ is a cubic function.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Assume a general form\n\nLet’s assume $ f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d $. We can test this form.\n\nBut let’s go back to the equation:\n\n$$\nf(x - y) + f(y - z) + f(z - x) + 3xyz = f(x + y) + f(y + z) + f(z + x)\n$$\n\nWe can try to find a specific function $ f(x) $ that satisfies the equation.\n\nLet’s try $ f(x) = x^3 $. Let’s check:\n\n- Left-hand side:  \n  $$\n  f(x - y) + f(y - z) + f(z - x) + 3xyz = (x - y)^3 + (y - z)^3 + (z - x)^3 + 3xyz\n  $$\n\n- Right-hand side:  \n  $$\n  f(x + y) + f(y + z) + f(z + x) = (x + y)^3 + (y + z)^3 + (z + x)^3\n  $$\n\nLet’s expand both sides.\n\n### Left-hand side:\n\n$$\n(x - y)^3 + (y - z)^3 + (z - x)^3\n= 3(x - y)(y - z)(z - x)\n$$\n\nSo LHS = $ 3(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) + 3xyz $\n\n### Right-hand side:\n\n$$\n(x + y)^3 + (y + z)^3 + (z + x)^3\n= 3(x + y)(y + z)(z + x)\n$$\n\nSo RHS = $ 3(x + y)(y + z)(z + x) $\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n$$\n3(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) + 3xyz = 3(x + y)(y + z)(z + x)\n$$\n\nDivide both sides by 3:\n\n$$\n(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) + xyz = (x + y)(y + z)(z + x)\n$$\n\nSo the equation simplifies to:\n\n$$\n(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) + xyz = (x + y)(y + z)(z + x)\n$$\n\nThis identity holds for all real $ x, y, z $. So this suggests that the function is:\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^3\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Final answer\n\nSo, $ f(x) = x^3 $.\n\nTherefore, the value of $ f(15) $ is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{15^3 = \\boxed{3375}}\n$$",
